From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 23:32:53 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] mshtml: Selection object, document.createRange,
 performance.now, window moves, getAttributeNode

Gaps of the IE9-IE11 script interface that made scripts fail:
- window.getSelection() and document.getSelection() gave E_NOTIMPL. They now
  return a Selection object (anchor/focus node and offset, isCollapsed,
  rangeCount, getRangeAt, addRange, removeRange, removeAllRanges, collapse,
  collapseToStart/End, selectAllChildren, deleteFromDocument, toString) on top
  of the engine's selection.
- document.createRange was not reachable from script (the document did not
  expose IDocumentRange).
- performance.now() (document mode 10+): milliseconds since the navigation
  started, with the fraction.
- window.moveTo/moveBy/resizeTo/resizeBy move and resize the window of the
  host browser (put_Left/Top/Width/Height of the IWebBrowser2 of the host); with
  no host browser they do nothing and return S_FALSE (the Windows tests have that
  for moveBy and resizeBy).
- element.getAttributeNode (document mode 9+) returned null for attributes
  that are only in the DOM (markup or setAttribute attributes without a
  property); the attribute node now reads its value from the DOM.

